Initial source audit:

- Lite public API includes `buildSubscriptionsForHeartbeat(Map)` in the pinned 5.5.1 artifact/source; it clears and rebuilds the retained heartbeat subscription set. The 5.3.3 checkout lacks that interface method, so all remaining source checks use the pinned commit.
- Existing Rust core already has QUERY_ASSIGNMENT/SET_MESSAGE_REQUEST_MODE and POP/ACK/batch-ACK/change-invisibility RPCs. Push rebalance currently detects POP assignments but skips activating them; the consumer crate has no Lite polling facade or receipt abstraction.
- Phase 13 Java fixture invokes Lite defaults/setters/heartbeat subscription construction, Push POP settings, `PopResult`, and `ExtraInfoUtil` receipt parsing. Fixture contents are in `fixtures/consumer/lite-pop.json`.

Oracle fixture generation attempts:

- Initial compile used a guessed MessageModel package and failed; corrected to `org.apache.rocketmq.remoting.protocol.heartbeat.MessageModel` from pinned source.
- Initial fixture called delegated `PullAPIWrapper` settings before start; the Java implementation dereferences an uninitialized wrapper in that lifecycle state. Removed those pre-start calls; the method signatures remain captured in the API inventory.
- The constructor's consume timestamp is time-dependent; fixture records whether it is within one second of the 30-minute default instead of storing the changing timestamp.

Current Phase 13 acceptance is not yet met. Continue with failing Rust cases before implementing Lite state, POP assignment/queue workers, and receipt operations. Keep local unit/fixture checks distinct from Phase 19 live Broker evidence.

